  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-22, in his own words:\n\n> Bug, hiding world origin axis, should not hide world plane/grid, that should hide seperatly.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe user turns off the world origin axes. The viewport grid (the world plane) disappears as well. The user has no way to hide the axes and keep the grid.\n\n## Expected\n\nTwo separate switches. \"Origin axes\" hides the axes only. \"Grid\" hides the grid only.\n\n## What the code says\n\n- The Display menu has two boxes: \"Grid\" (`show_grid`) and \"Origin axes\" (`show_world_axes`) in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/display_menu.rs`. The Browser pane has a third switch, \"Show world origin axes\" (`browser_pane.rs`), and the viewport bar has a fourth, the axes toggle (`viewport_bar.rs`). All three write `show_world_axes`.\n- The grid is drawn only when both flags are on: `if !state.show_world_axes || !state.show_grid { return ... }` in `crates/ui/src/interact.rs`. The comment there says that the grid uses the same switch as the triads. The doc comment of `show_grid` in `state.rs` says that the grid also needs `show_world_axes`.\n- The test `egui_app::tests::display_menu` checks only one direction: with the grid hidden, the axes stay. It does not check the other direction.\n- The issue #2818 (closed) added the \"Grid\" box. It was written so that the box \"hides the grid alone\". It did not make the axes switch independent of the grid.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe grid depends on `show_grid` only. The axes depend on `show_world_axes` only. Update the two comments. Add a test: with the axes hidden and the grid on, the grid is drawn.\n\n## Not changed\n\nThe saved view preferences keep both keys. A project that hid the axes before shows the grid again after the change. Say this in the changelog row.\n\nDone means: a structural test shows the grid drawn with the axes off, and the axes drawn with the grid off, from each of the three switches; the comments are correct.\n",
